That detail — "I just rename it for testing" — was the whole answer. Thank you for mentioning it even though it wasn't breaking your workflow.

**The rename never queued a save at all.** `RootNodeInfo` overrides `Name` only to attach the property-grid attributes, but the override assigned the backing field directly instead of going through the base's `SetField`:

```csharp
public override string Name
{
    get => _name;
    set => _name = value;   // no PropertyChanged raised
}
```

